{#-
  A document doc-class's table of contents (Stage 6c, design.md section 10.5).

  **Flat.** `toc.yml.j2` carries `children` and a precomputed indent because a
  version's navigation is a tree; a folder of PDFs is a list, and reusing that
  template would mean rendering a one-level tree to say so.

  `path` is the bare filename -- the file sits beside this one -- and `type` and
  `bytes` are the two figures AEM asked the item to carry. `bytes` goes through no
  `| yaml`: it is an integer, and quoting it would publish `"1234"`.

  `entries` arrives fully ordered from `sync/documents.py`: kind rank, then title.
  Nothing is sorted here. A template that ordered the list would be a second place
  the order is decided, and the one nobody tests.
-#}
# AEM table of contents{% if title %} for {{ title }}{% endif %}
# Generated by DocuShift (Stage 6) -- do not edit by hand.
items:
{% for entry in entries -%}
- title: {{ entry.title | yaml }}
  path: {{ entry.name | yaml }}
  type: {{ entry.type | yaml }}
  bytes: {{ entry.bytes }}
{% endfor -%}
